// Unsigned-artifact hold: pause a release while any artifact in it carries no
// valid signature. UNSIGNED_ARTIFACT_COUNT is the number of artifacts in the
// release under evaluation that the host could not verify a signature for.
// REGIME: release evaluation. Armed while the host is deciding whether a release
// may ship; it says nothing about systems already running.
// CONDITIONS: none in the rule. The host enumerates the artifacts, verifies the
// signatures, decides what counts as valid, and defines which release is under
// evaluation. Nano verifies no signature, sees no artifact and cannot stop a
// pipeline: this rule expresses the policy, it does not enforce it.
// INVALIDATION: every artifact verifying, so the count returns to zero. The rule
// does not latch; ending the hold and re-running the release are the host's job.
// SHAPE: 1m; fast enough not to delay a clean release, and the count only moves
// when the host re-verifies, so checking faster adds nothing.
// NOT trusted_route_guard: that pauses a running system that lost its trusted
// path. This one holds a release that has not shipped because its contents
// cannot be attributed to whoever was supposed to build them.
// CALIBRATED ON: policy, not data. The ceiling is one rather than a tolerance
// because a single unsigned artifact is exactly the one an attacker would
// substitute; there is no number of unattributed binaries that is safe to ship.
strategy UnsignedArtifactHold {

    agent SecurityDesk

    every 1m {

        if UNSIGNED_ARTIFACT_COUNT >= 1 {

            pause()

        }

    }

}
